Fix audio pops during voice volume changes with smooth ramping

The volume change command was causing audible pops because voice_volume
was being updated instantaneously, causing discontinuities in the audio
waveform. This commit implements smooth volume ramping to eliminate pops.

Changes:
- Add target_voice_volume field to ActiveSample and LiveInput structs
- Implement advance_voice_volume() method that ramps at ~0.001/frame
  (approximately 22ms for a full 0-1 transition at 44.1kHz)
- Update mix_sample_into_output() and mix_sample_with_pitch_correction()
  to advance volume ramping each frame
- Update mix_live_input_into_output() with the same ramping logic
- Update VoiceVolume command handler to set target volume for smooth
  ramping instead of instant change
- Also update live inputs when voice volume changes (previously only
  samples were updated)
- Add comprehensive tests for volume ramping behavior including:
  - Smooth transition verification
  - Rapid succession volume changes
  - Volume ramping during mixing
  - LiveInput volume ramping
  - No-change when at target

The smooth ramping ensures that rapid volume changes simply update the
target and the volume continues ramping smoothly toward the new target,
avoiding any discontinuities.

